From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:13:44 -0500
Subject: feat: only the Space on screen shows its icon in colour (S-548)

GitHub issue 122: at half strength in colour, the other Spaces' icons in
the switcher stood out about as much as the active one. The owner picked
the third of four rendered looks on 2026-11-20: every chip not on screen
shows its icon grey, at 35% (kInactiveGlyphAlpha), in the open row and
in the rail. The chip a drag would drop on stays in colour, and a chord
keeps the colour ChordColor picks for its contrast.

Only the glyph turns grey. The label draws into a layer of its own,
which the compositor greys; the chip's own background (a dot's disc, the
drop target's) keeps the Space's colour. The session badge (spaces B38)
gets a layer too, so it is still drawn over the glyph, and it keeps its
session's colour.

Tests: SpaceSwitchTest.OnlyTheSpaceOnScreenIsInColour,
IsolationMarkTest.TheBadgeKeepsItsColourOnAGreyChip.

Why: GitHub issue 122 asked for the Space on screen to stand out from
the others; the owner picked this look from four renders.
Removable when: never as behaviour.
